From 0000033000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <adn@x>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long CAL driver consent -- "tap to fire" (0033)

The 0029/0031/0032 cal sequencer arms a rep on engaged + no lead + near-straight + no rear-quarter
blind spot. But when those conditions align the car brakes ITSELF, uninitiated: a 2.2 s scripted
brake hold starts with no action by the owner. The reference-model review ranked DRIVER-CONSENT-
PER-REP the #1 mitigation for the rear-approach risk (the mirror is a 100+ m rear sensor): it
converts an uninitiated robot brake into a driver-INITIATED one.

0033 adds a driver-consent gate to ``CalSequencer``. Consent is SEPARATE, ADDITIVE and
FAIL-CLOSED: it can only ADD a pending/skip, never remove any existing veto (production gates, the
0031 budget mirror, the 0032 blind-spot veto all still apply on every frame).

  * ``conditions.consent_mode`` (or a top-level ``consent`` object) selects the policy:
      - ``off``  -- today's fully-autonomous behaviour. DEFAULT (backward compat). The ONLY
                    tap-free mode.
      - ``all``  -- every rep needs a tap.
      - ``high`` -- only reps at/above ``consent.min_level_lsb`` (default 22 = 0.22 g) need a tap.
    A MISSING mode is ``off``; a PRESENT-but-unrecognised mode coerces to ``all`` (strictest
    non-off), so a typo can never silently re-enable autonomous actuation.
  * When a rep is DUE and all conditions pass and consent is required, the sequencer does NOT
    actuate: it PARKS the rep (``state.pending``) and writes ``/data/fca11-cal/pending.json``
    (ADVISORY, for the superproject mici prompt). While a rep is parked the sequencer actuates
    NOTHING.
  * The tap is a FRESH, rep-bound ``/data/fca11-cal/consent.json`` = {rep_id, ts, accept}. The
    sequencer consumes it and fires ONLY if it is <= 2 s fresh, bound to THIS rep_id, accepted, AND
    every condition (incl. the 0032 blind-spot veto) and the 0031 budget STILL hold at the moment
    of the tap. Absent / malformed / stale / mismatched / non-accepted -> NEVER actuates.
  * The pending prompt EXPIRES after ``consent.timeout_s`` (default 8 s) if untouched and the rep
    is retried later (after a re-prompt hold-off). An explicit dismiss (accept=false) skips the rep
    for the rest of the session.
  * The consent channel: the ``pending.json`` / ``consent.json`` FILE pair (car layer <-> UI over
    /data), NOT a cereal/capnp field. Rationale: the car layer (card.py) runs in its own process and
    the cal sequencer state lives entirely in the file-based plan model already; a capnp field would
    couple four more files (custom.capnp, opendbc structs, card.py, helpers.py) into a schema change
    for a signal that is UI-only, per-prompt, and inherently ephemeral. The file route keeps the
    WHOLE cal feature in one place (cal_mode.py + /data/fca11-cal/) and keeps the fail-closed
    argument local and auditable. The UI also does not need a cereal subscription: it stats two
    small files (throttled) and never blocks rendering.

Python-only: no safety/ file, no panda change -> the panda FIRMWARE BYTES ARE UNCHANGED (no
reflash). Inert when cal mode is off (the sequencer is never reached); ``consent_mode=off`` is
byte-identical to the 0032 behaviour.

---
diff --git a/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/cal_mode.py b/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/cal_mode.py
index 3c060280..7d6f23dc 100644
--- a/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/cal_mode.py
+++ b/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/cal_mode.py
@@ -63,6 +63,33 @@ GATE + SAFETY
 * NO NEW AUTHORITY: the command envelope (<= 30 LSB, Warn=3 actuating shape, 50 Hz window, the
   same camera-mirror bytes) is a strict subset of what the production planner can already command.
 
+DRIVER CONSENT -- "TAP TO FIRE" (patch 0033)
+--------------------------------------------
+A rep is a real, 2.2 s scripted brake on a live road. The reference-model review ranked
+DRIVER-CONSENT-PER-REP the #1 mitigation for the rear-approach risk: it converts an uninitiated
+robot brake into a driver-INITIATED one. Consent is ADDITIVE and never weakens any existing veto
+(the production gates, the 0031 budget mirror, the 0032 blind-spot veto): it can only ADD a pending
+state and a tap requirement, never remove one.
+
+``conditions.consent_mode`` (or a top-level ``consent`` object) selects the policy:
+  * ``off``  -- today's fully-autonomous behaviour. DEFAULT for backward compatibility. This is the
+                ONLY mode that actuates without a tap.
+  * ``all``  -- every rep needs a tap.
+  * ``high`` -- only reps at/above ``consent.min_level_lsb`` (default 22 = 0.22 g) need a tap; the
+                lower-g reps stay automatic.
+A MISSING mode is ``off`` (compat); a PRESENT-but-unrecognised mode coerces to ``all`` (the strictest
+non-off mode), so a typo can never silently re-enable autonomous actuation (fail-closed).
+
+When a rep is DUE and every condition passes and consent is required for it, the sequencer does NOT
+actuate: it PARKS the rep (``pending``) and writes ``/data/fca11-cal/pending.json`` for the UI to show
+a prompt. The owner taps; the UI writes ``/data/fca11-cal/consent.json`` = {rep_id, ts, accept}. The
+sequencer consumes that file and, ONLY if it is FRESH (<= 2 s), bound to THIS rep_id, and accepted,
+RE-VERIFIES every condition (and the budget) at the instant of the tap and then fires. Anything else
+-- absent, malformed, stale, mismatched, non-accepted -- NEVER actuates. A parked rep EXPIRES after
+``consent.timeout_s`` (default 8 s) if untouched and is retried later; an explicit dismiss (accept =
+false) is honoured for the rest of the session. The pending file is ADVISORY (it only drives the
+prompt); the consent file is the sole authority and it is fail-closed.
+
 FILES (all under ``/data/fca11-cal/``; the module never touches anything else)
 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ``plan.json``      -- written ONCE (per revision) by the operator. The immutable matrix.
